{"units": [{"id": "polydakrytos-word2", "translation": "Πολυδάκρυτε [much-wept] in unprinted copies before πανδάκρυτε [all-wept], so πάνδυρτε [all-lamented] should be written: see πάνδυρτος [all-lamented]"}, {"id": "polydektes-orth1", "translation": "Polydektes"}, {"id": "polydektes-def1", "translation": "was the title of a play of Aeschylus, mentioned in the Catalogue. See on this name Thes. vol. 6 p. 1377."}, {"id": "polydonos-orth1", "translation": "much tossed"}, {"id": "polydonos-def1", "translation": "much tossed"}, {"id": "polydonos-note1", "translation": "Πολύ-δονον [much-tossed]"}, {"id": "polydonos-note2", "translation": "Φίλων πολύδονα σώ-μαθ᾽ [the much-tossed bodies of loved ones]"}, {"id": "polydonos-note3", "translation": "Thus Prienus for ἁλίδονα σώματά πολυβαφή [sea-tossed bodies, much-dyed]."}, {"id": "polydonos-quote1", "translation": "wandering"}, {"id": "polydonos-quote2", "translation": "sea-dyed"}, {"id": "polydonos-word1", "translation": "much-tossed"}, {"id": "polydonos-word2", "translation": "the much-tossed bodies of loved ones"}, {"id": "polydonos-word3", "translation": "Thus Prienus for sea-tossed bodies, much-dyed"}, {"id": "polydromos-orth1", "translation": "swift-running"}, {"id": "polydromos-def1", "translation": "swift-running"}, {"id": "polydromos-note1", "translation": "Πολυδρόμου [swift-running]"}, {"id": "polydromos-quote1", "translation": "exile"}, {"id": "polydromos-word1", "translation": "swift-running"}, {"id": "polyepes-orth1", "translation": "wordy"}, {"id": "polyepes-def1", "translation": "wordy"}, {"id": "polyepes-note1", "translation": "Πολυεπεῖς [wordy]"}, {"id": "polyepes-note2", "translation": "πολυετεῖς [many years old] in the Florence copy."}, {"id": "polyepes-note3", "translation": "The substantive πολυέπεια [wordiness] is used by writers of the middle period, as indicated in Thes. vol. 6 p. 1381; the adjective by no one except Aeschylus."}, {"id": "polyepes-quote1", "translation": "arts"}, {"id": "polyepes-word1", "translation": "wordy"}, {"id": "polyepes-word2", "translation": "many years old"}, {"id": "polyepes-word3", "translation": "The substantive wordiness is used by writers of the middle period, as indicated in Thes. vol. 6 p. 1381; the adjective by no one except Aeschylus"}, {"id": "polyeyktos-orth1", "translation": "much prayed for"}, {"id": "polyeyktos-def1", "translation": "much prayed for"}, {"id": "polyeyktos-note1", "translation": "Ὁ πᾶσιν φίλος καὶ [the friend of all and]"}, {"id": "polyeyktos-quote1", "translation": "much-prayed-for wealth"}, {"id": "polyeyktos-word1", "translation": "the friend of all and"}, {"id": "polyelakatos-orth1", "translation": "abounding in reeds"}, {"id": "polyelakatos-def1", "translation": "abounding in reeds"}, {"id": "polyelakatos-note1", "translation": "Τὸν κάλαμον τῶν βελῶν, φασὶ, καὶ Αἰσχύλος ἐν Αἴτναις (κορριγε Αἴτναιαις) τοὺς ποταμοὺς [the reed of the arrows, they say, and Aeschylus in Aetnae (correct Aetnaeae) the rivers]"}, {"id": "polyelakatos-note2", "translation": "Νον φλυβιος, σεδ τὰ τῶν ποταμῶν χείλη, υτ μονετ Μ. Σχμιδτιυς, κολλατα γλ. Χεσυχιυς, ἠλακάτη: δόναξ. ὁμοίως καὶ πολυηλάκατα τὰ τῶν ποταμῶν χείλη [not rivers, but the banks of rivers, as M. Schmidt advises, comparing Hesychius, ἠλακάτη: δόναξ [spindle: reed]. Similarly πολυηλάκατα [many-spindled] the banks of rivers]"}, {"id": "polyelakatos-quote1", "translation": "he says many-spindled"}, {"id": "polyelakatos-word1", "translation": "the reed of the arrows, they say, and Aeschylus in Aetnae (correct Aetnaeae) the rivers"}, {"id": "polyelakatos-word2", "translation": "not rivers, but the banks of rivers, as M. Schmidt advises, comparing Hesychius, spindle: reed. Similarly many-spindled the banks of rivers"}, {"id": "polytheos-orth1", "translation": "full of gods"}, {"id": "polytheos-def1", "translation": "full of gods"}, {"id": "polytheos-note1", "translation": "Ἐξ ἑδρᾶν [from the seats]"}, {"id": "polytheos-note2", "translation": "where Heimsoethius conjectured πανθέων [of all gods] because of the cretic of the strophic verse."}, {"id": "polytheos-quote1", "translation": "of many gods"}, {"id": "polytheos-word1", "translation": "from the seats"}, {"id": "polytheos-word2", "translation": "of all gods"}, {"id": "polythrenos-orth1", "translation": "much-lamenting"}, {"id": "polythrenos-def1", "translation": "much-lamenting"}, {"id": "polythrenos-note1", "translation": "Μεταμανθάνουσα δ᾽ ὕμνον Πριάμου πό-λις γεραιά [the ancient city learning anew the hymn of Priam]"}, {"id": "polythrenos-note2", "translation": "Πολύθρηνον [much-lamenting]"}, {"id": "polythrenos-quote1", "translation": "much-lamenting, greatly, I think, she groans"}, {"id": "polythrenos-quote2", "translation": "life"}, {"id": "polythrenos-word1", "translation": "the ancient city learning anew the hymn of Priam"}, {"id": "polythrenos-word2", "translation": "much-lamenting"}, {"id": "polythroos-orth1", "translation": "loud-shouting"}, {"id": "polythroos-def1", "translation": "loud-shouting"}, {"id": "polythroos-note1", "translation": "Μάταισι [with vain]"}, {"id": "polythroos-quote1", "translation": "loud-shouting"}, {"id": "polythroos-word1", "translation": "with vain"}, {"id": "polykanes-orth1", "translation": "slaying many"}, {"id": "polykanes-def1", "translation": "slaying many"}, {"id": "polykanes-note1", "translation": "Θυσίαι πα-τρὸς πολυκανεῖς βοτῶν [sacrifices of the father, slaying many sheep]"}, {"id": "polykanes-quote1", "translation": "of shepherds"}, {"id": "polykanes-word1", "translation": "sacrifices of the father, slaying many sheep"}, {"id": "polyklautos-orth1", "translation": "much-wept"}, {"id": "polyklautos-def1", "translation": "much-wept"}, {"id": "polyklautos-note1", "translation": "Ὦ πολύκλαυτε θανὼν [O much-wept one, having died]"}, {"id": "polyklautos-note2", "translation": "Τὴν πολυκλαύτην [the much-wept]"}, {"id": "polyklautos-note3", "translation": "Thus Porson for πολύκλαυτόν τ᾽ Ιφιγένειαν [and much-wept Iphigenia]."}, {"id": "polyklautos-quote1", "translation": "lord"}, {"id": "polyklautos-quote2", "translation": "Iphigenia"}, {"id": "polyklautos-word1", "translation": "O much-wept one, having died"}, {"id": "polyklautos-word2", "translation": "the much-wept"}, {"id": "polyklautos-word3", "translation": "Thus Porson for and much-wept Iphigenia"}, {"id": "polykoiranos-orth1", "translation": "ruling many"}, {"id": "polykoiranos-def1", "translation": "ruling many"}, {"id": "polykoiranos-note1", "translation": "Παι. Ἀτρέως [child of Atreus]"}, {"id": "polykoiranos-quote1", "translation": "ruler of many"}, {"id": "polykoiranos-word1", "translation": "child of Atreus"}, {"id": "polykrates-orth1", "translation": "very powerful"}, {"id": "polykrates-def1", "translation": "very powerful"}, {"id": "polykrates-note1", "translation": "Πολυκρατεῖς Ἀραὶ [very powerful Curses]"}, {"id": "polykrates-quote1", "translation": "of the dead"}, {"id": "polykrates-word1", "translation": "very powerful Curses"}, {"id": "polyktonos-orth1", "translation": "murderous"}, {"id": "polyktonos-def1", "translation": "murderous"}, {"id": "polyktonos-note1", "translation": "Τῶν πολυκτόνων γὰρ οὐκ ἄσκοποι [for not unobserving of the murderous]"}, {"id": "polyktonos-note2", "translation": "Μέγα σίνος [great harm]"}, {"id": "polyktonos-quote1", "translation": "gods"}, {"id": "polyktonos-quote2", "translation": "murderous"}, {"id": "polyktonos-word1", "translation": "for not unobserving of the murderous"}, {"id": "polyktonos-word2", "translation": "great harm"}, {"id": "polymitos-orth1", "translation": "woven with many threads"}, {"id": "polymitos-def1", "translation": "woven with many threads"}, {"id": "polymitos-note1", "translation": "as Pliny interprets it, H.N. 8, 48."}, {"id": "polymitos-note2", "translation": "Πολυ-μίτων πέπλων τ᾽ ἐπιλαβὰς [and the fastenings of many-threaded robes]"}, {"id": "polymitos-note3", "translation": "From Cratinus Pollux 7, 31 records it."}, {"id": "polymitos-quote1", "translation": "my"}, {"id": "polymitos-word1", "translation": "and the fastenings of many-threaded robes"}, {"id": "polymitos-word2", "translation": "From Cratinus Pollux"}, {"id": "polymnestos-orth1", "translation": "well-remembering"}, {"id": "polymnestos-def1", "translation": "well-remembering"}, {"id": "polymnestos-def2", "translation": "much remembered, celebrated"}]}